+## AGC 26.2 alpha23 - compiled dispatch and stable-diff runtime
+
+Alpha23 keeps the performance rule strict: Minecraft-visible logic stays ordered, while AGC reduces the cost of reaching that same result. This pass adds a compiled dispatch layer over the alpha22 tick-work compiler so helper work is assigned stable slots instead of repeatedly walking large decision chains.
+
+New runtime pieces:
+
+- `AGCScale23DispatchTable` compiles tick-local invisible helper jobs into stable dispatch slots. Visible Bukkit/world operations are never dispatched through worker slots.
+- `AGCNetworkStableDiffPlanner` builds immutable packet diff-vector plans for non-interactive fanout. It does not drop packets, share mutable packets, or reorder a connection stream.
+- `AGCChunkFrontierScheduler` converts chunk demand into FIFO-compatible frontiers. It never skips a player queue head and never changes Paper chunk completion order.
+- `AGCEntityVisibilityLattice` reduces tracker candidate planning with a read-only observer lattice. It never skips entity tick, AI, damage, interaction, or Bukkit entity events.
+- `AGCPluginCommitCoalescer` coalesces only plugin classification/ledger tickets; Bukkit-visible work remains ordered primary-thread commit.
+- `AGCWorldBarrierDAGCompiler` compiles read-only world prepare waves while keeping block/fluid/block-entity/entity/plugin barriers ordered.
+- `AGCWorkerRoutePlanner` reserves CPU/memory headroom for primary thread, plugins, Netty, GC and OS before routing any read-only helper work.
+
+New diagnostics/API: `/agc scale23`, `AGC.performance().scale23Plan(...)`, `AGCScale23Plan`, and seven new `AGCFeature` entries for the alpha23 algorithm layer.
